prompt:
You are a formal verification assistant. The following Dafny program fails Dafny verification.

=== PROGRAM ===
method is_anagram(s: string, t: string) returns (result: bool)
    requires |s| == |t|
    ensures (multiset(s) == multiset(t)) == result
{
    result := is_equal(multiset(s), multiset(t));
}


method is_equal(s: multiset<char>, t: multiset<char>) returns (result: bool)
    ensures (s == t) <==> result
{
    var s_removed := multiset{};
    var s_remaining := s;
    while (|s_remaining| > 0)
        invariant forall removed :: removed in s_removed ==> (removed in s &&
                                                              removed in t &&
                                                              s[removed] == t[removed])
    {
        var remaining :| remaining in s_remaining;
        if !(remaining in s &&
             remaining in t &&
             s[remaining] == t[remaining]) {
           return false; 
        }

        var temp := multiset{};
        s_removed := s_removed + temp[remaining := s[remaining]];
        s_remaining := s_remaining - temp[remaining := s[remaining]];
    }


    var t_removed := multiset{};
    var t_remaining := t;
    while (|t_remaining| > 0)
        invariant t_remaining == t - t_removed
        invariant forall removed :: removed in t_removed ==> (removed in s &&
                                                              removed in t &&
                                                              s[removed] == t[removed])
    {
        var remaining :| remaining in t_remaining;
        if !(remaining in s &&
             remaining in t &&
             s[remaining] == t[remaining]) {
           return false; 
        }

        var temp := multiset{};
        t_removed := t_removed + temp[remaining := t[remaining]];
        t_remaining := t_remaining - temp[remaining := t[remaining]];
    }

    return true;
}

=== DAFNY ERROR ===
program.dfy(23,11): Error: a postcondition could not be proved on this return path

program.dfy(10,21): Related location: this is the postcondition that could not be proved
   |
10 |     ensures (s == t) <==> result
   |                      ^^^^

Dafny program verifier finished with 1 verified, 1 error

=== COUNTEREXAMPLE ===
State: s == t.

Analyze the failure and respond with ONLY a valid JSON object — no explanation, no markdown, no code fences. Use exactly this structure:

{
  "spec_element": "<one of: requires | invariant | ensures>",
  "proof_obligation": "<one of: initiation | preservation | bridge>",
  "diagnosis": "<explanation of what broke and why>",
  "repair": "<the corrected Dafny specification line that restores the intended behavior>"
}

Definitions:
- requires: the precondition that must hold before the method executes
- invariant: the loop invariant that must hold throughout the loop
- ensures: the postcondition that the method must guarantee on return
- initiation: the precondition does not establish the invariant at loop entry
- preservation: the loop body does not maintain the invariant
- bridge: the invariant and loop exit condition do not imply the postcondition

raw_response:
{
  "spec_element": "invariant",
  "proof_obligation": "bridge",
  "diagnosis": "The first while loop lacks an invariant linking s_remaining, s_removed, and s. At loop exit (|s_remaining| == 0) the verifier only knows that elements in s_removed appear in both s and t with matching counts, but cannot conclude s == s_removed. Without s == s_removed and t == t_removed (the latter available via the second loop's invariant), the final return true cannot be bridged to the postcondition s == t <==> result.",
  "repair": "invariant s_remaining == s - s_removed"
}
